title: Recyclable, but really?
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

63% of US households can put a juice carton in the recycling bin. About 20% of cartons get recycled.

What does the word "recyclable" promise?

We presume it means that I can recycle 

Pieces:

* [[Tetra Pak]]: the paper comes back, the rest mostly doesn't
* [[Juice Pouch]]: nothing comes back
* [[Downcycling]]: what "recycled" often means
* [[Greenwashing]]: a true claim that misleads
* [[Rethinking the Recycling Symbol]]: one symbol, four meanings, and a graphic design problem
* [[Aluminum]]: the same metal, recyclable in a chair and lost in a carton
* The same question for compost: [[PLA]] is compostable only where there is a plant that can do it. Compostable where?

See [[Monstrous Hybrid]], [[Recycle]]
